    points: ['New A-rated combi boiler', 'New radiators with TRVs', 'All new pipework', 'Smart or programmable controls', 'Magnetic filter and inhibitor'] },
  { id: 'three-bed', tier: 'Family homes', name: '3-bed home', price: '£5,295', from: true, unit: 'full system, inc VAT',
    points: ['New A-rated boiler, combi or system', 'New radiators with TRVs', 'All new pipework', 'Smart or programmable controls', 'System cleaned to BS 7593', 'Old system taken away'] },
  { id: 'four-bed', tier: 'Larger Formby homes', popular: true, name: '4-bed home', price: '£6,295', from: true, unit: 'full system, inc VAT',
    points: ['System boiler sized for a bigger home', 'Upstairs and downstairs zones', 'New radiators with TRVs', 'Smart zone controls', 'Unvented cylinder priced at survey', 'Benchmark and gas safety checks'] },
  { id: 'combi-conversion', tier: 'Tank to combi', name: 'Combi conversion', price: '£2,890', from: true, unit: 'fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Cylinder system changed to a combi', 'Hot water cylinder and loft tanks removed', 'Keeps your radiators if they are sound', 'Usually 1 to 2 days'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does central heating installation cost in Formby?', a: 'A full new system starts from £4,495 for a 2-bed home, £5,295 for a 3-bed and £6,295 for a 4-bed, including VAT. Larger homes with zones, a cylinder or underfloor heating are priced at the free survey. The price we give you is fixed and in writing.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover all of Formby and L37?', a: 'Yes. We cover all of L37, including Freshfield and Formby Village. We also cover Hightown L38, Ainsdale PR8, Crosby L23, and Maghull and Lydiate L31.' },
  { q: 'Can you fit zone heating in my Formby home?', a: 'Yes. Many 4 and 5-bed Formby homes suit separate upstairs and downstairs zones, each with its own thermostat. Under Building Regulations, a home over 150 square metres needs at least two heating zones. We plan zones at the survey.' },
  { q: 'Can you connect underfloor heating to my central heating?', a: 'Yes. Wet underfloor heating in a kitchen extension can run off the boiler on its own zone, with its own thermostat. We plan it at the survey alongside the radiators. It is priced at the survey.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a system boiler or a combi in Formby?', a: 'A combi suits a home with one bathroom. A home with two or three bathrooms used at once usually needs a system boiler and an unvented cylinder. We test your mains pressure at the survey before we recommend one.' },
  { q: 'Are your engineers G3 qualified?', a: 'Yes. All our engineers are G3 qualified for unvented cylinders, which the law requires for this work. We fit, commission and service unvented cylinders. A yearly cylinder service is £120.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take?', a: 'A standard 3-bed system takes 3 to 5 days. A larger home with zones and a cylinder takes 5 to 7 days. A big renovation with underfloor heating can take 7 to 10 days. We agree dates at the survey.' },
  { q: 'What warranty do I get?', a: 'The boiler comes with a maker\'s warranty of 7 to 12 years, depending on the model. We register it for you. Our own work has a 12-month workmanship guarantee.' },
  { q: 'Do you offer finance?', a: 'No, we do not offer finance. You get a fixed written price, so you know the full cost before we start.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. All gas work is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register before they start.' },
];
---

