  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does central heating installation cost in Formby?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full new system starts from £4,495 for a 2-bed home, £5,295 for a 3-bed and £6,295 for a 4-bed, including VAT. Extra zones, a cylinder or underfloor heating are priced at the survey.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table stk">
          <thead><tr><th>Home</th><th>Typical radiators</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td data-label="Home"><strong>2-bed flat or cottage</strong></td><td data-label="Typical radiators">Up to 6</td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £4,495</td><td data-label="Typical time">2 to 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Home"><strong>3-bed semi</strong></td><td data-label="Typical radiators">7 to 10</td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £5,295</td><td data-label="Typical time">3 to 5 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Home"><strong>4-bed detached</strong></td><td data-label="Typical radiators">11 or more</td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £6,295</td><td data-label="Typical time">5 to 7 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td data-label="Home"><strong>Combi conversion</strong></td><td data-label="Typical radiators">Keeps your radiators</td><td data-label="Price, inc VAT">from £2,890</td><td data-label="Typical time">1 to 2 days</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>An unvented cylinder adds from £1,450 for 150 litres, or from £1,695 for 210 litres. Bigger homes may need 250 to 300 litres, from £1,995. See our <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-formby">Formby cylinder prices</a>.</p>
      <p>A 4-bed detached with zones, a cylinder and underfloor heating in an extension is a very different job from a 3-bed combi swap. We design it at the free survey. The price we give you is the price you pay.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="bigger-homes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What heating do larger Formby homes need?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Most Formby homes are 3 to 5-bed detached or semi-detached. Many are being extended. They need a system designed for the house, not a combi put where the old boiler was.</p>
      <h3>Zone heating</h3>
      <p>One thermostat for a 5-bed house heats every room the same. That wastes gas. Zones split the house, usually upstairs and downstairs. Each zone has its own thermostat and timer. Under Building Regulations, a home over 150 square metres needs at least two zones.</p>
      <h3>Underfloor heating in extensions</h3>
      <p>Many Formby owners want underfloor heating in a new kitchen or open-plan extension. A wet underfloor circuit can run off the boiler. It gets its own zone and thermostat, so the extension heats on its own. We fit this alongside the radiators as one job. It is common in Freshfield and Formby Village renovations.</p>
      <h3>System boilers and unvented cylinders</h3>
      <p>A combi struggles when two or three bathrooms run at once. A system boiler with an unvented cylinder gives mains-pressure hot water to every tap. All our engineers are G3 qualified, which the law requires for unvented cylinders. We size the boiler, cylinder and zones together at the survey.</p>
      <h3>Smart zone controls</h3>
      <p>We fit Nest and Hive controls. You set each zone from your phone and switch on the extension floor from the sofa. We set up the app and show you how it works. If the controls need new wiring, our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> does the electrical work.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Planning an extension or renovation?</strong> Book a free survey. It is the best time to add zones or underfloor heating.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="options">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for my Formby home?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">It depends on your bathrooms, the size of the house and what you have now. We tell you honestly at the survey.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A combi system</h3>
          <p>Best for flats, cottages and homes with one bathroom. Simple, compact and no tanks. From £4,495 for a full system.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A system boiler and cylinder</h3>
          <p>Best for homes with two or more bathrooms. Strong hot water to every tap at once. Common in larger L37 homes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-cols" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>A new boiler only</h3>
          <p>Best if your radiators and pipes work well. See <a href="/boiler-installation-formby">boiler installation in Formby</a> from £2,195.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>An upgrade</h3>
          <p>Best if some rooms are cold. Add <a href="/radiators-formby">radiators</a>, zones or a <a href="/power-flushing-formby">power flush</a> without starting again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Signs your home needs new central heating</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>One thermostat</strong> for a 4 or 5-bed home</li>
        <li><strong>Weak hot water</strong> in upstairs bathrooms</li>
        <li><strong>A new extension</strong> with no heating planned yet</li>
        <li><strong>Rooms that stay cold</strong> with the heating on</li>
        <li><strong>A poor EPC rating</strong> of D or lower, which buyers now ask about</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a new central heating system?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything you need for a working system. There are no hidden extras.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>New A-rated boiler</strong> from Baxi, Worcester Bosch or Vaillant, sized for your home</li>
        <li><strong>New radiators</strong>, each sized for its room, with TRVs</li>
        <li><strong>All new pipework</strong>, routed to keep it out of sight where we can</li>
        <li><strong>Zone valves and thermostats</strong> where your home needs zones</li>
        <li><strong>Smart or programmable controls</strong>, set up and shown to you</li>
        <li><strong>Magnetic filter, system clean and inhibitor</strong> to BS 7593</li>
        <li><strong>Balancing</strong> of every radiator and zone</li>
        <li><strong>Gas safety checks and Benchmark</strong> filled in on the day</li>
        <li><strong>Old boiler, radiators and tanks</strong> taken away</li>
        <li><strong>12-month workmanship guarantee</strong> on all our work</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="time">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does central heating installation take in Formby?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A standard home takes 3 to 5 days. A larger home with zones and a cylinder takes 5 to 7 days. A big renovation with underfloor heating can take 7 to 10 days.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free design survey.</strong> We check the layout, bathrooms, mains pressure, boiler spot and any extension plans. You get a fixed written price.</li>
        <li><strong>System planned.</strong> Zones, radiator sizes, cylinder size and any underfloor manifold are set before we start.</li>
        <li><strong>Install.</strong> We protect floors, run the pipes, hang the radiators and fit the cylinder. We tidy up each day.</li>
        <li><strong>Boiler and controls.</strong> Our Gas Safe registered engineers fit the boiler, flue and gas supply. We wire in the zone controls.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean, test, hand over.</strong> We clean the system, add inhibitor and fit the filter. We test every zone, commission the cylinder and show you the app.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="paperwork">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What paperwork and warranty do I get?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You get the maker's boiler warranty, our 12-month workmanship guarantee, the Benchmark checklist and a Building Regulations certificate.</p>
      <p>We register the boiler warranty for you and email your documents the same day. If we fit an unvented cylinder, you get its commissioning record too. The new boiler is notified to Building Control through the Gas Safe Register. Your certificate comes by post.</p>
      <p>Keep it all running with a yearly <a href="/boiler-service-formby">boiler service</a> at £120. An unvented cylinder service is £120.</p>
      <h3>Which areas near Formby do you cover?</h3>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Places and postcodes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Formby</strong></td><td>Formby, Freshfield and Formby Village, all L37</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Sefton coast and nearby</strong></td><td>Hightown L38, Ainsdale PR8, Crosby L23, Maghull and Lydiate L31</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Smell gas?</strong> Call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999 first. Then call us.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
